   - The page-title row above the stepper (page title text + small grid
     icon, per the Figma reference) is NOT built here — not mentioned in
     this message's scope ("ONLY the header + stepper"), so left for the
     same later pass that adds the warning banner/form fields.

   CurrentIndex/SelectedIndex history — the PIXEL-VERIFIED one-off snapshot
   this page used to render (CurrentIndex="4" + SelectedIndex="3", matching
   demo/ScreenB/TaskTwo_from_figma_design.png's literal frozen state, where
   Selected sits BEFORE Active — see AppStepper.razor's SelectedIndex doc
   comment and tokens.css's Stepper section for that full pixel history) is
   SUPERSEDED this pass by real click-driven navigation, per instruction.
   SelectedIndex is deliberately no longer passed here:
     - That override exists specifically to reproduce ONE static screenshot's
       non-standard snapshot state — it's not a general navigation rule, and
       nothing about real interactive stepping should reproduce "Selected
       lands behind Active" on every click.
     - Confirmed correct, not just complied with: live navigation's own
       spec — "stand on current, next one opens" — IS AppStepper's ORIGINAL,
       default formula (Selected = CurrentIndex + 1, GetState()'s fallback
       when SelectedIndex is unset). Passing the override here would fight
       the very behavior being wired in.
   Net effect: this page's on-load appearance no longer pixel-matches the
   frozen Figma export (that export captured one static point mid-flow, not
   the flow's start) — it now starts at index 0 and unlocks progressively
   via clicks instead, which is the correct behavior for a page that
   actually navigates rather than displaying one fixed screenshot. *@
